# Work Package — Medium Priority

## Objective

Complete the remaining UI Trust improvements by improving degraded-state messaging and warning consistency.

---

# Task 1 — User-Friendly Degraded State Tooltips

## Goal

Replace internal `queueDegradedReason` values with operator-friendly tooltips.

### Requirements

- Do not expose internal reason codes.
- Explain the operator impact in plain language.
- Provide the next action only when necessary.
- Keep tooltips brief and helpful.
- Do not repeat information already visible in the UI.
- Preserve raw reason codes for logs or diagnostics only.

---

# Task 2 — Display Management Warning Standardization

## Goal

Apply the established Warning standard to `useRefereeDisplayManagement.ts`.

### Requirements

Ensure warning messages use the existing UI Trust standards:

- Warning tone
- Amber styling
- Warning icon
- Standard timeout
- Consistent wording

Do not introduce new warning behaviors or severity levels.

---

# Validation

Before closing this work package:

- Run the full 57-test regression suite.
- Add E2E tests only if tooltip or warning behavior changes.
- Verify no raw degradation codes are visible to referees.
- Verify warning styling is consistent with the rest of the application.

---

# Success Criteria

This work package is complete when:

- Every degraded-state tooltip is written for operators.
- No internal degradation codes are exposed in the UI.
- Display Management follows the same warning standards as the rest of the application.
- All regression tests pass with no new issues introduced.
